  "name": "CALCITONIN",
  "code": "CTN",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Parameter</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Normal Range</strong> (may vary by lab)</th>\n<th><strong>Increased Calcitonin</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Decreased Calcitonin</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Calcitonin</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Men:</strong> &lt; 10 pg/mL <strong>Women:</strong> &lt; 5 pg/mL</td>\n<td>- <strong>Medullary thyroid carcinoma (MTC)</strong> &rarr; primary clinical use as a tumor marker - C-cell hyperplasia (precursor of MTC) - Other neuroendocrine tumors (rare) - Chronic kidney disease - Autoimmune thyroiditis - Proton pump inhibitor (PPI) therapy (can mildly increase)</td>\n<td>- Usually not clinically significant - Very low/undetectable levels are normal after <strong>total thyroidectomy for MTC</strong> (used to monitor recurrence)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"841\" data-end=\"989\">\n<p data-start=\"843\" data-end=\"989\"><strong data-start=\"843\" data-end=\"888\">Calcitonin is secreted by thyroid C-cells</strong> and regulates calcium by lowering serum calcium levels (minor role compared to PTH and Vitamin D).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"990\" data-end=\"1202\">\n<p data-start=\"992\" data-end=\"1013\">Main clinical role:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1016\" data-end=\"1202\">\n<li data-start=\"1016\" data-end=\"1086\">\n<p data-start=\"1018\" data-end=\"1086\"><strong data-start=\"1018\" data-end=\"1084\">Diagnosis and monitoring of Medullary Thyroid Carcinoma (MTC).</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1089\" data-end=\"1202\">\n<p data-start=\"1091\" data-end=\"1202\">A <strong data-start=\"1093\" data-end=\"1123\">stimulated calcitonin test</strong> (with calcium or pentagastrin) may be used when basal levels are borderline.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1203\" data-end=\"1338\">\n<p data-start=\"1205\" data-end=\"1338\">After surgery for MTC, <strong data-start=\"1228\" data-end=\"1280\">falling/undetectable calcitonin = good prognosis</strong>, whereas <strong data-start=\"1290\" data-end=\"1335\">rising calcitonin = recurrence/metastasis</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
